    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"Key Drivers of Groundwater Fluoride and Nitrate Pollution and Human Risk Assessment Near a Coal Mine: A Case Study in Northwest China","description":"In the Hongdunzi coal mining area, prolonged coal extraction has elevated F− and NO3− levels in groundwater, raising ecological and health concerns. This study integrated hydrochemical analyses and machine-learning methods to identify the most important variables in groundwater and evaluate the non-carcinogenic risks of contaminants through a risk assessment model. The random forest model outperformed the support vector regression model in predicting F− and NO3− concentrations, exhibiting superior generalization and capability in capturing complex hydrogeochemical processes. F− enrichment was closely associated with NO2−, well depth, K+, Na+, and SO42−, reflecting the combined influence of the redox environment, vertical hydrogeological conditions, and the effect of mining activities on prolonged water–rock interactions. In contrast, the NO3− concentration was primarily related to Cl−, NH4+, NO2−, and water level, underscoring the synergistic effect between agricultural inputs, mining-related nitrogen sources, and enhanced vertical hydraulic connectivity between aquifers. Health risk analysis showed that drinking water ingestion accounted for over 95% of the total risk, with children being more susceptible. NO3− posed higher health risks than F−, with some phreatic aquifer samples exceeding acceptable thresholds, while F− risks remained generally manageable but more pronounced in the confined aquifer. Targeted mitigation measures, including agricultural source control, calcium-rich water artificial recharge, ecological buffer construction, regulated groundwater abstraction, and in-situ remediation, are recommended. This study provides valuable insights and practical strategies for groundwater security and sustainable management in mining areas.","datePublished":"2026-09-04T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-04T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"1","pageEnd":"18","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10230-026-01141-9","keywords":["Groundwater pollution","Fluoride occurrence","Nitrate pollution","Random Forest","Public health","Mining activity","Geology","Water Quality/Water Pollution","Hydrogeology","Mineral Resources","Ecotoxicology","Industrial Pollution Prevention"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig3_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig4_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig5_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig6_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig7_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10230-026-01141-9/MediaObjects/10230_2026_1141_Fig8_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Mine Water and the Environment","issn":["1616-1068","1025-9112"],"@type":["Periodical"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer Berlin Heidelberg","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"Linjie Xie","affiliation":[{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"School of Water and Environment, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Subsurface Hydrology and Ecological Effects in Arid Region of the Ministry of Education, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Eco-Hydrology and Water Security in Arid and Semi-Arid Regions of the Ministry of Water Resources, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Peiyue Li","url":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8771-3369","affiliation":[{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"School of Water and Environment, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Subsurface Hydrology and Ecological Effects in Arid Region of the Ministry of Education, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Eco-Hydrology and Water Security in Arid and Semi-Arid Regions of the Ministry of Water Resources, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"peiyueli@chd.edu.cn","@type":"Person"},{"name":"Xiaohui Gao","affiliation":[{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"School of Water and Environment, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Subsurface Hydrology and Ecological Effects in Arid Region of the Ministry of Education, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"},{"name":"Chang’an University","address":{"name":"Key Laboratory of Eco-Hydrology and Water Security in Arid and Semi-Arid Regions of the Ministry of Water Resources, Chang’an University, Xi’an, China","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"}],"isAccessibleForFree":false,"hasPart":{"isAccessibleForFree":false,"cssSelector":".main-content","@type":"WebPageElement"},"@type":"ScholarlyArticle"},"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage"}</script>

        
        
